<div class="faults-list"><article class="fault" data-id="sysd"><button class="fault-pick" data-id="sysd"><span class="fault-mod">systemd</span><b>Igor crashes</b><p>The checked-in systemd unit restarts it after 10 s. That is configuration, not a promise of recovery time.</p></button></article><article class="fault" data-id="claude"><button class="fault-pick" data-id="claude"><span class="fault-mod">Claude API</span><b>Claude API error</b><p>Up to two SDK retries, then a plain-language reply instead of a crash.</p></button></article><article class="fault" data-id="cap"><button class="fault-pick" data-id="cap"><span class="fault-mod">Spend cap</span><b>Monthly cap reached</b><p>At conversation start Igor answers with a &#x27;Budget cap reached&#x27; message instead of a reply. Not a per-call check.</p></button></article><article class="fault" data-id="hc"><button class="fault-pick" data-id="hc"><span class="fault-mod">healthchecks.io</span><b>Heartbeat fails</b><p>Logged and shown as an error in /status. A missed heartbeat is what healthchecks.io watches for; alert delivery is not shown here.</p></button></article><article class="fault" data-id="siri"><button class="fault-pick" data-id="siri"><span class="fault-mod">Siri endpoint</span><b>Siri too slow</b><p>Siri gets an apology now; the answer follows in Telegram.</p></button></article><p class="failnote">Failure behaviour is taken from Igor's source code (checked 5 Nov 2026). It describes expected behaviour, not a live incident.</p></div>
<div class="info"><b>Tap any box ·</b> <span id="igor-arch-info">Each module explains itself when you tap or hover it. LEDs and pulses are illustration, not live status.</span></div>
<p class="talk"><b>In one sentence:</b> Igor is a Telegram assistant I run on a home Linux server: owner-only access, remote admin over Tailscale, memory in SQLite, Claude API calls under a monthly spend cap, and a heartbeat to healthchecks.io so I know if it stops.</p>
<noscript><p class="failnote">The interactive controls need JavaScript; the diagram and the connection list above still show the full picture.</p></noscript>
